+### 5.5 Optional holidays — list N, each employee takes M (task 186)
+
+E.g. six optional holidays in the year, any two per employee. There is **no selection table**:
+the holidays live in the holiday calendar, the "two" is a leave policy quota, and an employee's
+pick is an ordinary leave request — so approval, cancellation, the ledger, attendance and year
+close all work unchanged.
+
+**Set up:**
+
+1. **Holiday calendar** for the year: add the six days with type **Optional** (or
+   **Restricted** — both count). They stay working days for everyone else; only Public holidays
+   close the office.
+2. **Leave type**, e.g. `OH` "Optional Holiday": *Can be taken on* = **Optional holidays only**,
+   paid, half day off (the screen turns it off; halves are refused anyway), approval as the
+   organisation prefers.
+3. **Leave policy rule** for `OH`: **Yearly**, quantity **2**, credited at the start of the
+   year, leave year starting **January**, no carry forward, not encashable, **no proration**.
+
+**Enforced by the server:**
+
+- A request of an `OptionalHoliday` type may only cover dates that are Optional/Restricted
+  holidays **in the employee's own resolved calendar** (assignment calendar → location
+  calendar → all-locations calendar, the same chain the attendance resolver uses). Another
+  location's or another tenant's optional holiday is refused. Error code `optional_holiday_date`
+  in preview.
+- Whole days only; an optional holiday that falls on the employee's week-off is refused.
+- The quota is the ordinary balance gate; taking the same date twice is the overlap gate.
+- A rule for an `OptionalHoliday` type must be **Yearly with `reset_month = 1`** — saving
+  anything else is a `422`, and so is switching a type to the rule while one of its rules
+  doesn't fit. **Why January:** holiday calendars are per calendar year; on the tenant's April
+  leave-year fallback the year's holidays would span two leave years and an employee could take
+  the quota twice.
+- **Proration** isn't enforced, but leave it off: a mid-year joiner would get e.g. 0.83 days,
+  which can't be used for a whole-day holiday.
+
+The employee's apply form swaps the date range for a list of their optional holidays with what
+they've taken (`GET /leave/me/optional-holidays`, [api-and-pages §4.17](api-and-pages.md)).
+
 ---
 
