+### 4.17 `GET /api/v1/leave/me/optional-holidays`
+
+Self-service and ungated (task 186). `?year=` defaults to the current year. Lists the
+Optional/Restricted holidays in **the caller's own resolved calendar** — each date is resolved
+through the same calendar chain the day-type resolver uses, so another location's or another
+tenant's holidays never appear.
+
+```json
+{
+  "year": 2026, "leave_type_master_id": 9, "quota": "2.00", "used": "1.00", "pending": "0.00",
+  "available_balance": "1.00",
+  "holidays": [
+    { "holiday_detail_id": 41, "holiday_date": "2026-01-14", "name": "Pongal", "holiday_type": "Optional", "status": "Past" },
+    { "holiday_detail_id": 42, "holiday_date": "2026-11-01", "name": "Kannada Rajyotsava", "holiday_type": "Restricted", "status": "Taken" },
+    { "holiday_detail_id": 43, "holiday_date": "2026-12-24", "name": "Christmas Eve", "holiday_type": "Optional", "status": "Available" }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+- `status`: `Taken` (an Approved request of the OptionalHoliday type covers it), `Pending`, `Past`
+  (before today, not taken) or `Available`.
+- `leave_type_master_id` is the tenant's active `date_rule='OptionalHoliday'` type (lowest
+  display order); `null` when there is none — the list is then informational and `quota` is null.
+- `quota` is the resolved policy rule's `accrual_quantity`; null when no policy covers the caller.
+- A picker only — `POST /requests` re-checks the date ([admin-configuration §5.5](admin-configuration.md)).
